<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rogun Dam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rogun Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the Vakhsh river in central Tajikistan, designed to be among the tallest in the world at about 335 metres. Begun in the Soviet period in 1976, it was halted after independence; work resumed in 2016, and its first turbines began generating power in 2018. Downstream <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a> long opposed it over fears for its water supply.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rogun-dam.jpg" alt="Rogun Dam" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sosh19632 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rogun_Dam.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
